- name: iq2c
  id: epy_block
  parameters:
    _source_code: "\"\"\"Interleaved I,Q floats -> complex pairs (2:1).\n\nThe kyttar\
      \ sink emits a complex chain's recovered stream as INTERLEAVED\nI,Q float32\
      \ (its output port is always float); this embedded block\nreassembles gr_complex\
      \ for the constellation display. An embedded block\n(not blocks.float_to_complex)\
      \ on purpose: stock converter ids are chip-side\nsplice markers to the placeKYT\
      \ importer, and this display glue must stay\nhost-side.\"\"\"\nimport numpy\
      \ as np\nfrom gnuradio import gr\n\n\nclass blk(gr.decim_block):\n    def __init__(self):\n\
      \        gr.decim_block.__init__(self, name='IQ Pairs to Complex',\n       \
      \                         in_sig=[np.float32],\n                           \
      \     out_sig=[np.complex64], decim=2)\n\n    def work(self, input_items, output_items):\n\
      \        n = len(output_items[0])\n        x = input_items[0][:2 * n]\n    \
      \    output_items[0][:] = x[0::2] + 1j * x[1::2]\n        return n\n"
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: interleaved I,Q floats -> gr_complex (host-side display glue)
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
  states:
    _io_cache: ('IQ Pairs to Complex', 'blk', [], [('0', 'float', 1)], [('0', 'complex',
      1)], '', [])
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [1056, 464.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: phases
  id: epy_block
  parameters:
    _source_code: |
      """Convergence phase splitter — encode TIME as COLOR.

      The QT constellation sink repaints only when its whole size-buffer is
      full, so a single-stream display can never show WHERE the new points
      are. Instead, split each 600-symbol burst into three phase streams
      (early / adapting / converged) drawn as separately-colored overlays:
      one glance shows the early scatter (red), the pull-in (magenta) and
      the converged corners (green). Off-phase samples are parked outside
      the visible window (the sync sink needs equal-rate inputs).
      """
      import numpy as np
      from gnuradio import gr


      class blk(gr.sync_block):
          def __init__(self, burst=600, early=100, mid=250):
              gr.sync_block.__init__(self, name='Convergence Phases',
                                     in_sig=[np.complex64],
                                     out_sig=[np.complex64] * 3)
              self.burst = int(burst)
              self.early = int(early)
              self.mid = int(mid)
              self.k = 0
              self.park = 10 + 10j     # far outside the +-1.2 window

          def work(self, input_items, output_items):
              x = input_items[0]
              n = len(x)
              idx = (self.k + np.arange(n)) % self.burst
              bands = ((0, self.early), (self.early, self.mid),
                       (self.mid, self.burst))
              for p, (lo, hi) in enumerate(bands):
                  out = output_items[p]
                  out[:n] = self.park
                  m = (idx >= lo) & (idx < hi)
                  out[:n][m] = x[m]
              self.k = (self.k + n) % self.burst
              return n
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    burst: burst_len
    comment: splits each burst into early/adapting/converged streams so the
      constellation shows WHEN each point happened
    early: '100'
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    mid: '250'
    minoutbuf: '0'
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [1216, 452]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: errcurve
  id: epy_block
  parameters:
    _source_code: |
      """Convergence learning curve — |y - nearest decision point|, smoothed.

      The quantitative "it is getting better": per equalized symbol, the
      distance to the nearest QPSK decision point (+-0.7071 +-0.7071j),
      lightly EMA-smoothed so the decay reads as a curve. Restarts high at
      every burst boundary (the chip cold-starts per batch) and decays as
      the on-chip taps adapt.
      """
      import numpy as np
      from gnuradio import gr


      class blk(gr.sync_block):
          def __init__(self):
              gr.sync_block.__init__(self, name='Distance to Decision',
                                     in_sig=[np.complex64],
                                     out_sig=[np.float32])
              self.d = 0.70710678
              self.ema = 0.0

          def work(self, input_items, output_items):
              x = input_items[0]
              dec = (np.sign(x.real) * self.d
                     + 1j * np.sign(x.imag) * self.d)
              err = np.abs(x - dec).astype(np.float32)
              out = output_items[0]
              a = 0.15
              e = self.ema
              for i in range(len(err)):
                  e = (1.0 - a) * e + a * float(err[i])
                  out[i] = e
              self.ema = e
              return len(err)
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: the learning curve — smoothed distance to the nearest decision
      point, per symbol
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [1216, 600]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
